  "summary_en": "European Commission web page explaining how CEN-CENELEC JTC 21 develops harmonised standards supporting the EU AI Act's high-risk requirements. It covers the ten standardisation request areas, voluntary use with presumption of conformity, the first draft standard prEN 18286, and international alignment with ISO/IEC SC 42.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Commission requested CEN and CENELEC to develop standards in ten areas, including risk management, cybersecurity and conformity assessment.",
   "Use of harmonised standards is voluntary but gives presumption of conformity once cited in the Official Journal.",
   "prEN 18286 (AI quality management system) entered public enquiry on 30 October 2025.",
   "An 'international first' approach lets aligned international standards become European harmonised standards.",
   "Standards aim to give legal certainty, reduce compliance costs and set global benchmarks."
